1341	     *  full 30 days past its due-by plus its grade's grace days ({@code grade}: its person's grade in force on its
1342	     *  date), the late percent in force on that boundary date (that day plus 30, 60, 90 ... days) of the figure
1343	     *  plus the charges of the boundaries before it (compounding), rounded as the claim rounds, added up; 0.00 when not overdue, it has no figure, it is a correction or its late charge was waived. While a
1344	     *  statement binds the claim with a late charge, it is that charge, whatever the sheet's today. */
1345	    public static BigDecimal lateCharge(Claim claim, BigDecimal figure, Sheet sheet, String grade) {
1346	        BigDecimal none = BigDecimal.ZERO.setScale(2);
1347	        if (!claim.getStatus().isOpen() || claim.isDeferredOn(sheet.getToday())) {
1348	            return none;
1349	        }
1350	        // A statement binds the late charge with the figure: while bound, it no longer follows the sheet's today.
1351	        if (claim.isBound() && claim.getBoundLate() != null && !claim.isCorrection() && !claim.isWaived()) {
1352	            return claim.getBoundLate();
